{
  "duration": 76.039,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.119,
      "end": 1.899,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.519,
      "end": 3.699,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.179,
      "end": 7.419,
      "text": "Now, in this problem, we are given that the downstream speed of a boat"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.879,
      "end": 8.019,
      "text": "is"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.46,
      "end": 10.199,
      "text": "27 kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.92,
      "end": 13.199,
      "text": "Also, the speed of the boat in still water"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.739,
      "end": 15.239,
      "text": "is 22 kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.819,
      "end": 18.799,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the upstream speed of the boat."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.219,
      "end": 21.959,
      "text": "Now, before solving, let us understand one simple concept."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.399,
      "end": 24.239,
      "text": "When a boat moves downstream,"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.719,
      "end": 26.739,
      "text": "the current helps the boat."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.119,
      "end": 30.0,
      "text": "So downstream speed is equal to speed in still water plus"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.42,
      "end": 31.279,
      "text": "speed of the current."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.659,
      "end": 38.479,
      "text": "We can also write this as speed of the current is equal to downstream speed minus speed in still water."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.879,
      "end": 41.959,
      "text": "Now, we already know the downstream speed and the speed in still water."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.52,
      "end": 43.399,
      "text": "Putting the values,"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.759,
      "end": 44.84,
      "text": "speed of the current is equal to"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.2,
      "end": 46.7,
      "text": "27 minus 22."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.139,
      "end": 48.879,
      "text": "This gives us five kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.319,
      "end": 52.659,
      "text": "Now that we know the speed of the current, we can find the upstream speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.099,
      "end": 54.36,
      "text": "Be very sure about one thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.699,
      "end": 62.399,
      "text": "When a boat moves upstream, the current moves against the boat. So upstream speed is equal to speed in still water minus speed of the current."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.899,
      "end": 66.619,
      "text": "Putting the values, upstream speed is equal to 22 minus 5."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.059,
      "end": 69.019,
      "text": "This gives us 17 kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.459,
      "end": 73.239,
      "text": "So the upstream speed of the boat is 17 kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.639,
      "end": 76.039,
      "text": "Hence, the correct answer is option D."
    }
  ],
